WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:02.375
I was honored that you
asked me to write the forward,

00:00:02.417 --> 00:00:03.708
but when you first asked me
to write the forward,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.959
the first thing I said was,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.458
"Girl!
You don't need a forward.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.959
Everybody knows who you are."

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.166
And I wrote
what I believe in my heart,

00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:14.417
I said that your words
healed our wounds

00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:16.583
and resurrected our spirits.

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:19.375
I think it was a shot
of light, you know?

00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:21.166
It was just like, "Whoa!"

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:24.792
An infusion of light
came into people's lives.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:29.166
What's magnificent about
this poem when you analyze it,

00:00:29.208 --> 00:00:32.583
there isn't a word
that is wasted.

00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:35.583
I'm a poetry reader
and have been for years,

00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:38.792
but my favorite passage

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.583
or piece of the poem
is when you say,

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.375
"We braved the belly
of the beast,

00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:49.083
we learned that quiet
isn't always peace,

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.708
and the norms and notions
of what just is,

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.166
isn't always justice.

00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:57.959
And yet the dawn is ours.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.166
Before we knew it,
somehow we do it.

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:05.792
Somehow we weathered
and witnessed a nation

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:11.166
that isn't broken,
but simply unfinished."

00:01:11.208 --> 00:01:13.166
I think that saying
our country isn't broken,

00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:15.792
it's just unfinished
is really hopeful,

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.041
and hope is something

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:19.583
we really need
more of right now,

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.959
and you obviously wanted
people to feel that

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.417
when you wrote this.

00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:27.375
What did you want the takeaway

00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:29.375
ultimately
from the poem to be?

00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.166
I wanted that to be
the takeaway,

00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:32.959
which is why I'm so glad
that you just read it.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.166
Which for me, I think,
looking at our democracy

00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:38.959
as something that's
unfinished is both hopeful,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.041
but it's also reflective.

00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.959
It's also interrogative.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.166
Meaning that it both
says we have work to do

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:47.792
and we can accomplish it.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:51.166
In the poem, I wanted
to speak of hope and unity,

00:01:51.208 --> 00:01:52.959
but it had to be rooted

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.000
in a sense of purpose
and dignity.

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:57.166
Because I think unity

00:01:57.208 --> 00:02:00.583
for the purpose of unity
without interrogation

00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:03.041
can just be
toxic mob mentality.

00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:04.375
It's not thinking about

00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:06.792
what are the reasons
that we're linking arms?

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.792
So I wanted to really
underscore this idea

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.792
that the American project
is a process

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.625
and it's not something
that I think

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.375
we've arrived at yet
as a country,

00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:17.959
but something
that we can continue

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.166
to labor for out of love.

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:23.166
Well, as a 23-year-old,

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:28.959
to have such discernment

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.166
and great perspective

00:02:32.208 --> 00:02:34.458
on everything
that's happened,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.375
and particularly everything
that's happened in recent years

00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:41.041
with the country's
divisiveness,

00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:44.375
how starkly divided
we all have become,

00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:48.583
how cancel culture
has affected almost everyone,

00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:51.834
how the world literally
shifted in front of us

00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:53.166
during the pandemic,

00:02:53.208 --> 00:02:56.583
but you were able
to do it one poem.

00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:59.959
When you say, "And, yes,
we are far from polished,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.166
far from pristine,
but this doesn't mean

00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:05.792
we're striving to form
a union that is perfect."

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:08.166
Which I think people
need to be reminded of,

00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:09.959
because we keep hearing
"a more perfect union."

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.792
We've heard that for years.

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:12.875
"But this doesn't mean
we're striving

00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.583
to form a union
that is perfect.

00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:18.208
We are striving to forge
our union with purpose."

